\\subsection*{Deflection angle}

\\begin{definition}[Angle between planar vectors]
\\label{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:angleBetween}
\\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.angleBetween}
\\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:Plane}
The angle between two planar vectors,
"'$'"\\arccos\\"'!'"\\big(\\langle a, b\\rangle / (\\lVert a \\rVert \\lVert b
\\rVert)\\big) \\in [0, \\pi]"'$.
'"\\end{definition}

\\begin{theorem}[Deflection magnitude and formula]
\\label{thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:signed_deflection_eq_formula}
\\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.signed_deflection_eq_formula}
\\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:angleBetween, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:IsAsymptoticRelativeVelocity, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:initialDirection, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:eccentricitySq, thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:orbit_eq_conic, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:CoulombScatteringData}
Any asymptotic relative velocity satisfies
"'$'"\\lVert u_\\infty \\rVert = \\sqrt{2E/m_{\\mathrm{red}}}"'$ and
$'"\\mathrm{angleBetween}\\ \\hat u_0\\ u_\\infty
= \\pi - 2\\arctan\\"'!'"\\big(1/\\sqrt{\\varepsilon"'^2 - 1}'"\\big)"'$.
Contains the sign/orientation input but no numeric deflection value.
'"\\end{theorem}
\\begin{proof}
The magnitude follows from the energy law at infinity, where the Coulomb
term vanishes and "'$E = '"\\tfrac12 m_{\\mathrm{red}} \\lVert u_\\infty \\rVert"'^2$.
For the direction, the hyperbola of
'"\\cref{thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:orbit_eq_conic} with
"'$'"\\varepsilon > 1"'$ has asymptote directions making the acute angle
$'"\\arctan\\sqrt{\\varepsilon"'^2 - 1}$ with the symmetry axis; traversed outward
from periapsis, the total change of direction between the incoming line and
the outgoing asymptote is
$'"\\pi - 2\\arctan\\"'!'"\\big(1/\\sqrt{\\varepsilon"'^2-1}'"\\big)"'$, read off on the
branch side recorded in
'"\\cref{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:IsAsymptoticRelativeVelocity}.
\\end{proof}

\\begin{definition}[Signed deflection]
\\label{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:signedDeflection}
\\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.signedDeflection}
\\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:angleBetween, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:initialDirection, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:Plane, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:CoulombScatteringData, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:RelativeVelocityVector}
The oriented (signed) deflection angle of the scattering, in radians:
"'$'"\\pm\\, \\mathrm{angleBetween}\\ \\hat u_0\\ u_\\infty"'$ with sign $+1$ when the
deflection is counterclockwise from the initial line of motion of $e''^+$
($0 '"\\le \\mathrm{perp}\\ \\hat u_0\\ u_\\infty"'$) and $-1$ when clockwise.  The
Fig.-1b orientation selects the clockwise case.
'"\\end{definition}

\\begin{definition}[Radians to degrees]
\\label{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:radiansToDegrees}
\\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.radiansToDegrees}
